# Screen-space effects and flat sprites in stereo (#22, #58), on the simulated headset with the Index's optics
# (index.vrsim: its asymmetric field of view, 5 degrees between the eyes) and the test save mvp-new-game:
#   .\scripts\dev\smoke-test.ps1 -VrSim index -Save mvp-new-game -Sequence stereo-effects
# One section per kind. `stereo-fx place <kind> <ahead> <right> <up>` puts a test effect that many meters from the
# head through the engine's own path (a light with a flare, fire and rune-flare particles, a fog emitter, a still
# particle); @stereo judges the change from a base shot to the effect's shot as the two eyes see it
# (stereo-check-lib.ps1): pairing, both eyes covered, the depth from the disparity (in front, at its distance), one
# height in both eyes, and for the single sprite the same size; a fade over both whole eyes; an overlay at infinity.
# Each fixed kind is shot a second time with `stereo-fx legacy on` - drawn per eye as before #22 - and the leg that
# must catch it has to fail.
@sim index
@args --loadslot 0
@save mvp-new-game

@until state eq GAMEPLAY 60s
@until vr.sim.timelineFrame ge 270 60s       # 3 s in: past the level's fade-in (TRAPS.md)
@until vr.head.source eq hmd 30s
@until notifications eq 0 60s                # the save's tutorial hint expires by game time: no HUD change between shots
@assert vr.stereo.active eq true
@assert vr.sim.view.cant eq 5
@assert stereoFx.legacy eq false

# The head turns 30 degrees left, to the cell's back corner: away from the barred door, whose torch flickers over
# everything near it from frame to frame. Every effect is placed from there, inside the cell
vr-sim head rot 30 0 0
@frames 10

# --- A billboard: one still particle 0.8 m away and 30 degrees left of the view, where the canted eyes' own screen
# squares differ most (the eyes overlap only within 37.5 degrees of the middle)
@shot billboard-base
stereo-fx place billboard 0.693 -0.4 0
@frames 10
@assert stereoFx.kind eq billboard
@shot billboard
@stereo billboard-base billboard sprite
stereo-fx legacy on
@frames 3
@shot billboard-legacy
@stereo billboard-base billboard-legacy sprite fails size
stereo-fx legacy off
stereo-fx clear
@frames 10

# --- A light's flare (renderLightFlares): a light with a flare and next to no reach, 0.8 m ahead
@shot flare-base
stereo-fx place flare 0.8 0 0
@wait 500                                    # the flare fades in once the light is seen (updateLightFlares)
@shot flare
@stereo flare-base flare fx
stereo-fx clear
@wait 500

# --- Fire: the particles of a torch's flame, 1.2 m ahead and a little low
@shot fire-base
stereo-fx place fire 1.2 0 -0.15
@wait 800
@shot fire
@stereo fire-base fire fx
stereo-fx clear
@wait 1700                                   # the last flames die (1.5 s at most)

# --- Magic: the rune flares the rune trail leaves at the hand (#43), 0.8 m ahead
@shot magic-base
stereo-fx place magic 0.8 0 0
@wait 800
@shot magic
@stereo magic-base magic fx
stereo-fx clear
@wait 3500                                   # rune flares live up to 3.2 s

# --- Fog: a level fog emitter's smoke, 1 m ahead
@shot fog-base
stereo-fx place fog 1 0 0
@wait 1500
@shot fog
@stereo fog-base fog fx
stereo-fx clear
@wait 5500                                   # fog puffs live up to twice the emitter's 2.5 s

# --- A scripted fade (worldfade) to white: over each eye's whole view, not only the flat frame's quad in the middle
@shot fade-base
worldfade out 300 1 1 1
@wait 800
@shot fade
@stereo fade-base fade view
stereo-fx legacy on
@frames 3
@shot fade-legacy
@stereo fade-base fade-legacy view fails covered
stereo-fx legacy off
worldfade in 300
@wait 800

# --- A full-view overlay: Magic Sight's red vignette, one head-locked image at infinity for both eyes. The spell also
# tints the world (the arm near the eyes most): the base is the spell with the overlay hidden, so the change is the
# overlay alone
spellcast -fsm 5 magic_sight self
@wait 500                                    # the cast's text stays on the HUD: base and shot are 6 frames apart, both have it
stereo-fx overlays off
@frames 3
@shot sight-base
stereo-fx overlays on
@frames 3
@shot sight
@stereo sight-base sight infinity
stereo-fx legacy on
@frames 3
@shot sight-legacy
@stereo sight-base sight-legacy infinity fails parallax
stereo-fx legacy off
